Found this related to that, but not sure if this was what I recalled, because this describes Windows having higher resolution than Linux 😄 (maybe I had filesystem timestamps precision in mind) https://github.com/golang/go/blob/go1.23.6/src/time/time.go#L83-L90

```go
// # Timer Resolution
//
// [Timer] resolution varies depending on the Go runtime, the operating system
// and the underlying hardware.
// On Unix, the resolution is ~1ms.
// On Windows version 1803 and newer, the resolution is ~0.5ms.
// On older Windows versions, the default resolution is ~16ms, but
// a higher resolution may be requested using [golang.org/x/sys/windows.TimeBeginPeriod].
```
